From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johan Walles <johan.walles@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 07:13:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] apple-gmux: restore the display switch before the GPUs resume

With force_igd, suspending with the screen on gives a black screen
after resume, every time. Turning the screen off and on again brings
the picture back.

On a MacBookPro16,1 at least, the firmware switches the panel to the
discrete GPU during S3. gmux_resume() switches it back, but the gmux is
a PNP device and resumes after the PCI GPUs. So i915 resumes first and
fails eDP link training on a panel that is switched away.

Restore the switch in .resume_early instead, which runs before any
.resume callback. Do the same for thaw and restore, which also went
through gmux_resume() before.

Restoring early is not enough by itself: right after the switch, the
panel doesn't answer on the AUX channel. On a MacBookPro16,1, waiting
100 ms after the switch was too short and 175 ms was enough. Wait
200 ms, the eDP maximum from panel power on until AUX works (T3). Only
wait on T2 Macs, and only if the firmware actually changed the switch,
so other resumes don't get slower.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Johan Walles <johan.walles@gmail.com>
---
Tested on a MacBookPro16,1 with the t2linux 7.2.8 kernel and
force_igd=y, S3 with the screen on (rtcwake -m mem -s 20): 4 out of 4
resumes came back with a picture. A debug build showed the gmux
display port reading 4 (iGPU) before suspend and 5 (dGPU) in
resume_early, every time. Hibernation and pre-T2 Macs are untested.

 drivers/platform/x86/apple-gmux.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 35 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/apple-gmux.c b/drivers/platform/x86/apple-gmux.c
index 656191d..4f14cab 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/apple-gmux.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/apple-gmux.c
@@ -765,13 +765,44 @@ static int gmux_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The firmware may switch the display to the discrete GPU during suspend.
+ * Switch it back before the GPU drivers resume, otherwise the integrated GPU
+ * fails to train the eDP link and the screen stays black.
+ */
+static int gmux_resume_early(struct device *dev)
+{
+	struct pnp_dev *pnp = to_pnp_dev(dev);
+	struct apple_gmux_data *gmux_data = pnp_get_drvdata(pnp);
+	bool is_mmio = gmux_data->config == &apple_gmux_mmio;
+	bool display_changed = false;
+	bool is_discrete;
+
+	if (is_mmio) {
+		is_discrete = gmux_read8(gmux_data, GMUX_PORT_SWITCH_DISPLAY) & 1;
+		display_changed = is_discrete !=
+			(gmux_data->switch_state_display == VGA_SWITCHEROO_DIS);
+	}
+
+	gmux_write_switch_state(gmux_data);
+
+	/*
+	 * On T2 Macs the panel doesn't answer on the AUX channel right after a
+	 * switch. On a MacBookPro16,1, 100 ms was too short and 175 ms enough.
+	 * Wait the eDP maximum from panel power on until AUX works (T3).
+	 */
+	if (display_changed)
+		msleep(200);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int gmux_resume(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct pnp_dev *pnp = to_pnp_dev(dev);
 	struct apple_gmux_data *gmux_data = pnp_get_drvdata(pnp);
 
 	gmux_enable_interrupts(gmux_data);
-	gmux_write_switch_state(gmux_data);
 	if (gmux_data->power_state == VGA_SWITCHEROO_OFF)
 		gmux_set_discrete_state(gmux_data, gmux_data->power_state);
 	return 0;
@@ -1037,6 +1068,9 @@ static const struct pnp_device_id gmux_device_ids[] = {
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops gmux_dev_pm_ops = {
 	.suspend = gmux_suspend,
+	.resume_early = gmux_resume_early,
+	.thaw_early = gmux_resume_early,
+	.restore_early = gmux_resume_early,
 	.resume = gmux_resume,
 };
 
-- 
2.53.0

